a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nNorthwestern Baca County in southeastern Colorado...\nEast central Las Animas County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 400 PM MDT.\n\n* At 321 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Pritchett, or\n20 miles west of Springfield, moving north at 25 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage\nto roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nPritchett.","ends":"2026-08-15T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Baca, CO; Las Animas, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0ff4841412016799b75cd2cac5e810454f89ae8a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0ff4841412016799b75cd2cac5e810454f89ae8a.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 15 at 3:05PM MDT until August 15 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"FFWPUB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSouthwestern Las Animas County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 600 PM MDT.\n\n* At 305 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain\nhave fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 1.25 to 2 inches in 1\nhour. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nTrinidad.","ends":"2026-08-15T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Las Animas, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ba2eb9de7ddbccb5a74e42f28558d2d7023b292a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ba2eb9de7ddbccb5a74e42f28558d2d7023b292a.001.1"},